bient Chi. Only one attempt to absorb Chi may be made per night, and a talisman may hold a maximum number of Chi Points equal to the dots in the Background (so, a three-dot jade talisman allows three dice to absorb Chi and may store a maximum of three Chi points at once). Subsequently, by touching the talisman and spending a turn in concentration, the vampire may utilize this Chi. Chi from a talisman may be used in normal fashion, to power Disciplines, heal wounds, etc. The vampire may still spend only as much Chi per turn as his Dharma rating allows. Talismans of true jade are exceedingly rare and greatly prized. You may have to defend your talisman against rapacious rivals. Occasionally, talismans are used as prizes in duels and gambling contests, but these contests must be of great consequence to merit such a stake.<br /> \u2022 One Chi Point<br /> \u2022\u2022 Two Chi Points<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022 Three Chi Points<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Four Chi Points<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Five Chi Points\u200b<br /> <br /> Land of Eight Million Dreams detailed the idea about Jade weapons; just as the Kithain are sensitive to Cold Iron, the shinma/hsien, the &quot;Little Gods&quot; can be sensitive to Jade. If the proper ritual awakens the chi of the jade it can cause aggravated wounds to the hsien.<br /> It should be stated that even ordinary mortals, even with no training, can attune jade through prayer and meditation. Jade is widely known to be of protection against spirits and the hisiem are still spirits even if they are trapped in human bodies.<br /> The Shih (the demon hunters of the Middle Kingdom) know this and often carry jade weapons.<br /> However, jade is also a power item for hsien - it can increase their magic, and many powerful treasures are made of Jade. Slightly paradoxical - but it works. Basically what it comes down to is - Jade has power. Anything with power is a two edged sword, this is why they have Jade Talisman: True Jade in Land of Eight Million Dreams<br /> Hengeyokai: Shapeshifters of the East mentions a few Jade Fetish or Talens but actually these are like other Werewolf things, somethat that is made out of Jade and atuned with a ritual or gift.<br /> <br /> In short, Jade is... well jade somebody properly atuned, you can buy it anywhere as a mineral, have an artisan to carve it and if you know the ritual, atune it<br /> The confusion\u200b comes from Wraith: The Oblivion:<br /> <b>White Jade</b> of Wraith is a &quot;Jade&quot; manufactured from the plasm of ghosts in the Yellow Springs. It is used to manufacture Artifacts in the same way that soulforging is used in Stygia. White Jade is made through a specific skill in the Way of the Artisan arcanos, and can only be created out of a wraith drained of all Willpower. Artifacts constructed from White Jade are less durable than artifacts constructed from <b>True Jade</b>, but it is far easier to acquire and therefore far cheaper.<br /> True Jade is is a more solid and durable form of Jade found in the Dark Kingdom of Jade, it is basically Relic Jade - a relic is a memory given shape in the Underworld that can survive for centuries. In this case some Jade. But compared to the white Jade made from plasm, even with the added relegious and cultural significance of Jade... it is rare. Very rare. Not to mention It is similar to Stygian Steel and causes aggravated damage...<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> Personally I tend to use a bit of a hosue rule to seperate the two kind of True Jade<br /> The Wraith True Jade is a relic of a Jade<br /> The &quot;mortal&quot; True Jade is a Jade that Jade spirit been &quot;awakened&quot; with a ritual</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you so much for the thorough answer! I really appreciate the time you put into your reply!<br /> So from what it sounds to be, Jade is often one of those gemstones that are often thought to have powers in the east?<br /> <img src=\"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/41WIWTO0D6L._SR600%2C315_PIWhiteStrip%2CBottomLeft%2C0%2C35_SCLZZZZZZZ_FMpng_BG255%2C255%2C255.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25177-lirbo","name":"Lirbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25177_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-24T10:04:10-07:00","id":1521334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lirbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1521218-a-little-question-about-jade-kindred-of-the-east?p=1521329#post1521329\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So from what it sounds to be, Jade is often one of those gemstones that are often thought to have powers in the east?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yes<br /> The power of jade for any shen, particularly a Kuei-jin, cannot be overemphasized. Jade acts as a lodestone for meditative and spiritual energies, as a receptacle for elements of the soul and as a tangible connection to the Yin and Yang Worlds.<br /> For example from the Companion, <b>Taste of Jade</b>, a Lvl 8 Jade Shintai power attune a piece of ordinary jade to Chi energies, turning it into a piece of True Jade for a time. Kuei-jin who have mastered this power are frequently adorned with jade from head to toe, and each piece of green stone is a focus for powerful Chi energies that they can call upon with only a thought.<br /> <br /> The <b>Imbuing the Jade </b>ritual enables Kuei-jin to imbue jade with properties that allow the gem\u2019s possessor to cross into the spirit worlds or utilize dragon lines. The vampire crafts jade replicas \u2014 tiny likenesses of the Kuei-jin \u2014 for use when following in the crab\u2019s footsteps, whereas she carves small boats for use when riding the dragon\u2019s tongue.<br /> <br /> \u200bJade is very special material in the Middle Kingdom. Jade is a &quot;Soul Substance&quot;. Vapable if protecting the soul from the various elements. It is generally considered ti bring luck. Jade also preserves life, extends life, and purifies the male spirit. The colour and quality of jade can make differences in how i can be used, as deffense or even as a weapon.<br /> To &quot;attune&quot; a Jade usually you need to spend a Yin or Yang Chi.<br /> <br /> <b>Blue and Green Jade</b> is used for defense, it requires spending of one Yin Chi in order to properly ward an entrance with blue or green jade.<br /> <b>Yellow and Gray Jade</b> is usable either deffense or attack; either color adds damage to a hand-to-hand strike against a shen (collective term for supernatural beings) if the holder expends one Yin Chi. The attacker rolls Wits + Occult (difficulty 7); for each success the aggressor inflicts one health level of lethal damage. For defenses, the holder spends one Yang Chi and the player rolls Wits + Occult (difficulty 7). Each success negates one health level of mystical damage (Disciplines, the claws of shen, etc.) from one attack.<br /> <b>White Jade</b> is used for warding against the shen by atuning with Yang Chi - ghost even take damage if try to enter a warded area<br /> <b>Black Jade </b>is a weapon and requires Yin Chi to awaken. Once awakened, the stone causes aggravated damage on all attacks against shen for one night.<br /> <b>Red Jade</b> brings luck, by spending a Yin and a Yang Chi to empower the red jade. Once per story the character wearing empowered red jade can reroll a botch in either offensive or defensive combat. Empowered red jade remains &quot;awakened&quot; indefinitely though, at the Storyteller's discretion, it may need another sacrifice of life force in order to bring luck.<br /> <b>Yu Ying Jade</b> is awesome, for 2 Yin Chi and 2 Yang Chi to dedicate the jade to you, it returns the favor one hundredfold. - a bit hyperbole, but it indeed replenish the individual's Chi by absorbing latent Chi from the world<br /> <br /> With ritual, or Discipline, or meditation and atuning, a simple piece of Jade could be very usefull<br /> Bit of course, the \u200bcolour and quality of jade is important!<br /> The people of the Middle Kingdom believed and still belives in the Jade's power because... well it have that power^^ - Even without attunement more often than not<br /> Especially if it was a high quality Jade carved with a master artisan and blessed by a priest - but even without that a piece could be usefull, even jade powder could &quot;cause troubles&quot; for the Shen<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-24T15:26:34-07:00","id":1521351,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1521218-a-little-question-about-jade-kindred-of-the-east?p=1521334#post1521334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes<br /> The power of jade for any shen, particularly a Kuei-jin, cannot be overemphasized. Jade acts as a lodestone for meditative and spiritual energies, as a receptacle for elements of the soul and as a tangible connection to the Yin and Yang Worlds.<br /> For example from the Companion, <b>Taste of Jade</b>, a Lvl 8 Jade Shintai power attune a piece of ordinary jade to Chi energies, turning it into a piece of True Jade for a time. Kuei-jin who have mastered this power are frequently adorned with jade from head to toe, and each piece of green stone is a focus for powerful Chi energies that they can call upon with only a thought.<br /> <br /> The <b>Imbuing the Jade </b>ritual enables Kuei-jin to imbue jade with properties that allow the gem\u2019s possessor to cross into the spirit worlds or utilize dragon lines. The vampire crafts jade replicas \u2014 tiny likenesses of the Kuei-jin \u2014 for use when following in the crab\u2019s footsteps, whereas she carves small boats for use when riding the dragon\u2019s tongue.<br /> <br /> \u200bJade is very special material in the Middle Kingdom. Jade is a &quot;Soul Substance&quot;. Vapable if protecting the soul from the various elements. It is generally considered ti bring luck. Jade also preserves life, extends life, and purifies the male spirit. The colour and quality of jade can make differences in how i can be used, as deffense or even as a weapon.<br /> To &quot;attune&quot; a Jade usually you need to spend a Yin or Yang Chi.<br /> <br /> <b>Blue and Green Jade</b> is used for defense, it requires spending of one Yin Chi in order to properly ward an entrance with blue or green jade.<br /> <b>Yellow and Gray Jade</b> is usable either deffense or attack; either color adds damage to a hand-to-hand strike against a shen (collective term for supernatural beings) if the holder expends one Yin Chi. The attacker rolls Wits + Occult (difficulty 7); for each success the aggressor inflicts one health level of lethal damage. For defenses, the holder spends one Yang Chi and the player rolls Wits + Occult (difficulty 7). Each success negates one health level of mystical damage (Disciplines, the claws of shen, etc.) from one attack.<br /> <b>White Jade</b> is used for warding against the shen by atuning with Yang Chi - ghost even take damage if try to enter a warded area<br /> <b>Black Jade </b>is a weapon and requires Yin Chi to awaken. Once awakened, the stone causes aggravated damage on all attacks against shen for one night.<br /> <b>Red Jade</b> brings luck, by spending a Yin and a Yang Chi to empower the red jade. Once per story the character wearing empowered red jade can reroll a botch in either offensive or defensive combat. Empowered red jade remains &quot;awakened&quot; indefinitely though, at the Storyteller's discretion, it may need another sacrifice of life force in order to bring luck.<br /> <b>Yu Ying Jade</b> is awesome, for 2 Yin Chi and 2 Yang Chi to dedicate the jade to you, it returns the favor one hundredfold. - a bit hyperbole, but it indeed replenish the individual's Chi by absorbing latent Chi from the world<br /> <br /> With ritual, or Discipline, or meditation and atuning, a simple piece of Jade could be very usefull<br /> Bit of course, the \u200bcolour and quality of jade is important!<br /> The people of the Middle Kingdom believed and still belives in the Jade's power because... well it have that power^^ - Even without attunement more often than not<br /> Especially if it was a high quality Jade carved with a master artisan and blessed by a priest - but even without that a piece could be usefull, even jade powder could &quot;cause troubles&quot; for the Shen</div> </div> </div> </div>I see! So from what I can understand, Jade can be purchased in many places in the Middle Kingdom as it is rather common (depending on the color).<br /> Jade can be activated with the usage with the infusion of Chi (either Yin, or Yang, depending on the color).<br /> <br /> True Jade however, is much more rare, and in addition to the regular powers of Jade, it can also store Chi points, which can be used normally. True Jade is essentially Jade that has turned into a Relic in the Underworld (just like any other object of great significance can turn into a Relic in the Underworld).<br /> <br /> Please correct me if I got anything wrong &lt;3<br /> <br /> One thing that I am not sure about, is what you previously mentioned: &quot;The &quot;mortal&quot; True Jade is a Jade that Jade spirit been &quot;awakened&quot; with a ritual&quot;.<br /> I was wondering if that's simply the concept of Spirit awakening like there is in MTA. And if so, how can mortals do this, are there any mechanics? I'm asking because I'm running a huge crossover where it might become a necessity.<br /> <br /> Lastly, can Kin-jin have any use of Jade? Or even True Jade if they somehow happen to get their Barbarian hands on it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25177-lirbo","name":"Lirbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25177_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-25T02:00:18-07:00","id":1521367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lirbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1521218-a-little-question-about-jade-kindred-of-the-east?p=1521351#post1521351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One thing that I am not sure about, is what you previously mentioned: &quot;The &quot;mortal&quot; True Jade is a Jade that Jade spirit been &quot;awakened&quot; with a ritual&quot;.<br /> I was wondering if that's simply the concept of Spirit awakening like there is in MTA. And if so, how can mortals do this, are there any mechanics? I'm asking because I'm running a huge crossover where it might become a necessity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Simple<br /> Relic is a term used by Wraiths to describe objects across the Shroud who are not formed by souls - things that inspired great passion in life, and which linger on in death.<br /> No longer in existence in the Skinlands, a relic is a memory given shape in the Underworld that can survive for centuries. It is a term that can apply to any item or device which crosses the Shroud with an Enfant, and they can be anything of value to that specific wraith, but usually have a symbolic tie to an individual or group of individuals.<br /> Most relics are ideals in some fashion and are generally tied to a wraith's self-image and may have special capacities associated with that.<br /> These items are a significant source of wealth in Underworld society, and are commonly bartered between the dead.<br /> Some of the most valuable relics have also been fashioned into artifacts.<br /> The reverse object of a relic is a phylactery from Mummy: The Resurrection; something in the world of the living into which a mummy can bind the power of the underworld, quasi an earthly manifestation of a relic.<br /> Now White Jade (Tiger Jade) is a kind of Tremolite Jade which is a variety of Nephrite, that's usually white, off-white, or cream in colour. White Jade is a gemstone that holds a lot of meaning and plenty of healing properties. White Jade has been used with this purpose for hundreds of years. It is believed to have a calming and soothing effect on the mind and body, promoting peace, harmony, and tranquility. It is often used in meditation practices and is thought to help individuals achieve a greater sense of awareness and spiritual awakening.<br /> BUT<br /> The White Jade of Wraith:the Oblivion, the Dark Kingdom of Jade is a &quot;Jade&quot; manufactured from the plasm of ghosts in the Yellow Springs. It is used to manufacture Artifacts in the same way that soulforging is used in Stygia. White Jade is made through a specific skill in the Way of the Artisan arcanos, and can only be created out of a wraith drained of all Willpower. Artifacts constructed from White Jade are less durable than artifacts constructed from True Jade, but it is far easier to acquire and therefore far cheaper.<br /> The True Jade of Wraith:the Oblivion, the Dark Kingdom of Jade is a more solid and durable form of Jade found in the Dark Kingdom of Jade, it is basically Relic Jade<br /> BUT (again^^)<br /> There is a &quot;mortal&quot; True Jade, like how there is a mortal world' White Jade and with Taste of Jade, a Lvl 8 Jade Shintai power you can attune a piece of ordinary jade to Chi energies, turning it into a piece of True Jade for a time.<br /> Obviously the power won't turn the ordinary Jade in to a Relic for a time<br /> Actually it is stated in the Companion as with any other wraithly matter, relics and artifacts of the Underworld cannot survive in the Land of the Living; if you try to bring over such object? It simply disperses in a puff of insubstantial plasm.<br /> So this two are two different things in my humble opinion<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lirbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1521218-a-little-question-about-jade-kindred-of-the-east?p=1521351#post1521351\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Lastly, can Kin-jin have any use of Jade? Or even True Jade if they somehow happen to get their Barbarian hands on it?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> For crossover porpuses it is stated Werewolf Rage and Gnosis can be compared to Yang and Yin Chi energy, respectively. Typical Werewolves have effective Chi pools of 25 points, though, due to their incredibly strong life forces just shapeshifters simply isn't able to channel all of its bodily Chi, and this excess can be drained by a Kuei-jin through the usual means<br /> <br /> With Vampire?<br /> <br /> Well usually they don't have faintest idea what Hun and P'o is (tho' P'o in a sense the Beast) Yin, Yang and Demon Chi is and how to use it - but since they are so undead, they could be considered heavily and parmanently Yin\u200b imbalanced, full of Yin Chi - so they can't really use, atune and awaken Jade by its own (but like any mortal could use simple jade, like them)<br /> Luckly(?) they are ideal pawns of the Yama Kings and even Akuma (or for some strange unfathomable reason a Kuei-Jin even) and may recieve some &quot;gift&quot; that is usable, for example Black Jade requires Yin Chi to awaken and once awakened, the stone causes aggravated damage on all attacks against shen for one night. So it is possible a Kuei-jin/Akuma/Yama King servant awoke a katana made out of black jade and gives it to the Kin-jin, &quot;This night you will be a mighty warrior...&quot; or a Red Jade talisman to bring luck<br /> Depends of the Jade, really\u200b - considering their Yin\u200b imbalance I would treat the Kin-jin as the Kuei-Jin when a Yin and Yang chi encounters (if you want, toss in the mix the Demon Chi of Yomi, the Tainted Chi and the Yugen, also called Golden Chi of the Hsien/Shinma - The Kuei-Jin vallue Yugen after all, hence the cold relationship between the Little Gods and the Kuei-Jin)<br /> Remember, the Kuei-Jin's body is basically an alchemical powerplant fueled by Chi and more often than not, several types are not necessarily compatible - same could be applied to the parmanently Yin\u200b imbalanced, full of Yin Chi Kin-Jin\u200b<br /> <br /> Worth to mention, on Blood &amp; Silk p. 158 there is a &quot;gossip&quot;, not a 100% fact, just &quot;rumors&quot; about the Salubri, the spawns of Zao-Lat and about their potential to awaken their P'o and start their Dharmic journey<br /> It have a lot of ground actually; aside the whole Saulot is two, the White Worm, his P'o and the one, his Hun that is wandering around, and his Devil-Tigerish behavior and mentality when he created the Baali, <i>Chi</i>'<i>iu Muh </i>is the key here, what Saulot/Zao-Lat &quot;have stolen&quot; and refined in to a signiture discipline is almost the same-version of the Wan Kuei Discipline to the point, the Watcher Valeren in Dark Ages 20th Anniversary Edition have the fifth level of power called Soul's Breath <b>- </b>Subsist on mortals' breaths instead of blood, or steal blood and power from other supernatural creatures through their breath<br /> Not as effective as the Dharmic &quot;benefit&quot;, but still<br /> Such a stransformed Salubri probably would be able to use Jade<br /> Then again it wouldn't really be a Kin-jin anymore... but a Kuei-jin\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":