f Nephrite, that's usually white, off-white, or cream in colour. White Jade is a gemstone that holds a lot of meaning and plenty of healing properties. White Jade has been used with this purpose for hundreds of years. It is believed to have a calming and soothing effect on the mind and body, promoting peace, harmony, and tranquility. It is often used in meditation practices and is thought to help individuals achieve a greater sense of awareness and spiritual awakening.<br /> BUT<br /> The White Jade of Wraith:the Oblivion, the Dark Kingdom of Jade is a &quot;Jade&quot; manufactured from the plasm of ghosts in the Yellow Springs. It is used to manufacture Artifacts in the same way that soulforging is used in Stygia. White Jade is made through a specific skill in the Way of the Artisan arcanos, and can only be created out of a wraith drained of all Willpower. Artifacts constructed from White Jade are less durable than artifacts constructed from True Jade, but it is far easier to acquire and therefore far cheaper.<br /> The True Jade of Wraith:the Oblivion, the Dark Kingdom of Jade is a more solid and durable form of Jade found in the Dark Kingdom of Jade, it is basically Relic Jade<br /> BUT (again^^)<br /> There is a &quot;mortal&quot; True Jade, like how there is a mortal world' White Jade and with Taste of Jade, a Lvl 8 Jade Shintai power you can attune a piece of ordinary jade to Chi energies, turning it into a piece of True Jade for a time.<br /> Obviously the power won't turn the ordinary Jade in to a Relic for a time<br /> Actually it is stated in the Companion as with any other wraithly matter, relics and artifacts of the Underworld cannot survive in the Land of the Living; if you try to bring over such object? It simply disperses in a puff of insubstantial plasm.<br /> So this two are two different things in my humble opinion<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> \u200b<br /> For crossover porpuses it is stated Werewolf Rage and Gnosis can be compared to Yang and Yin Chi energy, respectively. Typical Werewolves have effective Chi pools of 25 points, though, due to their incredibly strong life forces just shapeshifters simply isn't able to channel all of its bodily Chi, and this excess can be drained by a Kuei-jin through the usual means<br /> <br /> With Vampire?<br /> <br /> Well usually they don't have faintest idea what Hun and P'o is (tho' P'o in a sense the Beast) Yin, Yang and Demon Chi is and how to use it - but since they are so undead, they could be considered heavily and parmanently Yin\u200b imbalanced, full of Yin Chi - so they can't really use, atune and awaken Jade by its own (but like any mortal could use simple jade, like them)<br /> Luckly(?) they are ideal pawns of the Yama Kings and even Akuma (or for some strange unfathomable reason a Kuei-Jin even) and may recieve some &quot;gift&quot; that is usable, for example Black Jade requires Yin Chi to awaken and once awakened, the stone causes aggravated damage on all attacks against shen for one night. So it is possible a Kuei-jin/Akuma/Yama King servant awoke a katana made out of black jade and gives it to the Kin-jin, &quot;This night you will be a mighty warrior...&quot; or a Red Jade talisman to bring luck<br /> Depends of the Jade, really\u200b - considering their Yin\u200b imbalance I would treat the Kin-jin as the Kuei-Jin when a Yin and Yang chi encounters (if you want, toss in the mix the Demon Chi of Yomi, the Tainted Chi and the Yugen, also called Golden Chi of the Hsien/Shinma - The Kuei-Jin vallue Yugen after all, hence the cold relationship between the Little Gods and the Kuei-Jin)<br /> Remember, the Kuei-Jin's body is basically an alchemical powerplant fueled by Chi and more often than not, several types are not necessarily compatible - same could be applied to the parmanently Yin\u200b imbalanced, full of Yin Chi Kin-Jin\u200b<br /> <br /> Worth to mention, on Blood &amp; Silk p. 158 there is a &quot;gossip&quot;, not a 100% fact, just &quot;rumors&quot; about the Salubri, the spawns of Zao-Lat and about their potential to awaken their P'o and start their Dharmic journey<br /> It have a lot of ground actually; aside the whole Saulot is two, the White Worm, his P'o and the one, his Hun that is wandering around, and his Devil-Tigerish behavior and mentality when he created the Baali, <i>Chi</i>'<i>iu Muh </i>is the key here, what Saulot/Zao-Lat &quot;have stolen&quot; and refined in to a signiture discipline is almost the same-version of the Wan Kuei Discipline to the point, the Watcher Valeren in Dark Ages 20th Anniversary Edition have the fifth level of power called Soul's Breath <b>- </b>Subsist on mortals' breaths instead of blood, or steal blood and power from other supernatural creatures through their breath<br /> Not as effective as the Dharmic &quot;benefit&quot;, but still<br /> Such a stransformed Salubri probably would be able to use Jade<br /> Then again it wouldn't really be a Kin-jin anymore... but a Kuei-jin\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, thank you so much for the time and effort you put into your reply. It's truly not something that I take for granted. Your input about the Kin-jin part was actually beyond what I expected. In fact, I might explore that area now too. Thank you for that!<br /> <br /> As for True Jade, after rereading your replies countless times before crafting this response to avoid asking repetitive questions (as I'm genuinely trying to respect your time), I think I understand what you mean better. True Jade in the Underworld is essentially normal Jade that has turned into a Relic in that realm. True Jade in the living world is Jade that has had its spirit awakened through a ritual or other means (for example, the Spirit sphere of mages, or that Taste of Jade ritual that somewhat turns Jade into True Jade).<br /> <br /> If that's the case, I assume that even the highest levels of Kuei-jin cannot fully awaken Jade. They primarily have to rely on finding existing True Jade, therefore its price is incredibly high.<br /> <br /> Do I understand you correctly?<br /> \u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25177-lirbo","name":"Lirbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25177_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-25T08:55:25-07:00","id":1521381,"title":"","content":"Yes<br /> You are correct <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> (Mostly because In the 4th Age there were more powerfull Kuei-Jin around and even the several Shintai were different &quot;purer&quot;, just like how reaching the <i>Hundred Clouds</i>\u200b were easier to achieve<br /> The 5th Age we are currently in is darker, harder, and we are in the brink of the Sixth Age when the Demon Emperor grabs the throne of the August Personage of Jade (and when he is defeated comes the Seventh Age and everything becme progressively better untill the 12th Age that will be the 1st again, as the Wheel turns)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-25T10:36:57-07:00","id":1521395,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1521218-a-little-question-about-jade-kindred-of-the-east?p=1521381#post1521381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes<br /> You are correct <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> (Mostly because In the 4th Age there were more powerfull Kuei-Jin around and even the several Shintai were different &quot;purer&quot;, just like how reaching the <i>Hundred Clouds</i>\u200b were easier to achieve<br /> The 5th Age we are currently in is darker, harder, and we are in the brink of the Sixth Age when the Demon Emperor grabs the throne of the August Personage of Jade (and when he is defeated comes the Seventh Age and everything becme progressively better untill the 12th Age that will be the 1st again, as the Wheel turns)</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, thank you so much for your assistance!<br /> One final question, though. I have limited access to the Companion book as I lend a physical copy from a friend.<br /> Did you happen to access your books through DriveThruRPG by any chance? I'm asking because before I was about to check out I noticed this:<br /> <img title=\"image.png\" data-tempid=\"temp_1296_1692984840494_362\" data-align=\"none\" data-size=\"full\" loading=\"lazy\" border=\"0\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1296\" alt=\"\" data-fullsize-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1296\" data-thumb-url=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=1296&amp;type=thumb\" data-title=\"Click on the image to see the original version\" data-caption=\"image.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment thumbnail js-need-data-att-update js-lightbox-participant\" itemprop=\"image\"/><br /> \u200bDo you happen to know the quality condition of the PDF?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25177-lirbo","name":"Lirbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25177_1.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"48"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-08-25T10:46:28-07:00","id":1521397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lirbo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1521218-a-little-question-about-jade-kindred-of-the-east?p=1521395#post1521395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did you happen to access your books through DriveThruRPG by any chance?</div> </div> </div> </div>I have physical copies <br /> Don't really know anything about the PDF conditions <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}